@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;">

    <h1 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom:35px;">Last updated: @DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("MMMM yyyy")</p>

    <div class="card" style="padding:35px;line-height:1.8;">

        <h3 class="section-title">What we collect</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            A username. Registered accounts also have a password; guest sessions started
            from the home page have a display name instead, and no password. Optionally,
            a profile: bio, country, date of birth, interests, language and a generated
            avatar &mdash; every one of those is yours to leave blank. We also store the
            text messages you send during a conversation, and basic counts such as how
            many conversations you have had and how long you have spent on voice calls.
        </p>

        <h3 class="section-title">Age</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            @AppSettings.AppName is open to anyone, and we do not ask your age to let you
            in. You can record a date of birth on your profile if you want to, and it is
            optional &mdash; when you do give one, we ask that it be at least
            @AppSettings.MinimumAge. Nothing here is verified, so please use your own
            judgement about who you are talking to: conversations are with strangers, and
            we cannot tell you who is on the other end.
        </p>

        <h3 class="section-title">Voice calls</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Voice runs over WebRTC. Your browser asks for microphone permission only when
            you start or accept a call. <strong>We never record or store call audio.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Where your two networks allow it, audio travels directly between you and the
            other participant. Often they do not &mdash; mobile networks and many home
            routers block a direct connection &mdash; and in that case the audio is
            forwarded through a third-party relay server (a TURN relay) so the call can
            connect at all. The relay passes the audio through in real time and does not
            record it, but it is a third party in the path, and we would rather say so
            than describe every call as private end-to-end when it is not.
        </p>

        <h3 class="section-title">Conversations &amp; matching</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            You are paired with a random stranger. Any interests and language saved on
            your profile are used to prefer a better match, but never to identify you to
            the other person &mdash; they see your display name and any interests you
            both share, nothing else.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">
            Text messages are stored in our database so the conversation works and so
            reports can be reviewed. They are kept until the account is deleted; they are
            not sold, and not shared with third parties.
        </p>

        <h3 class="section-title">Reporting &amp; moderation</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            You can report anyone you are matched with, once per conversation. Reports are
            used to review and, where necessary, restrict accounts. Repeated reports may
            result in a temporary restriction on starting new chats, and serious or
            repeated cases in a permanent suspension.
        </p>

        <h3 class="section-title">Your data</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">
            You can edit or clear most of your profile at any time from your account.
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(AppSettings.ContactEmail))
            {
                <text>
                    To have your account and its associated data removed entirely, email
                    <a href="mailto:@AppSettings.ContactEmail">@AppSettings.ContactEmail</a>.
                </text>
            }
            else
            {
                <text>
                    To have your account and its associated data removed entirely, get in
                    touch with us.
                </text>
            }
        </p>

    </div>

</div>
